---
description: Default all new Kyth runtime features to Rust and Tauri, not Python
alwaysApply: true
---

# Rust/Tauri Is the Default

For all new Kyth product features, use Rust for runtime, service, CLI, and
system-integration code. Use the existing Tauri/React Hub shell for desktop UI.

- Do not introduce Python as a new installed runtime authority, launcher,
  service, desktop UI, or production implementation.
- Keep user-visible desktop workflows in the existing Tauri/React Hub when they
  need a UI; expose only typed, narrowly scoped Rust Tauri commands.
- New privileged behavior belongs behind the existing Rust privileged boundary;
  do not add a generic shell or process-execution bridge.
- Python may remain only for existing compatibility/parity fixtures, tests, or
  an explicitly approved exception. Document any exception and its removal or
  review condition in the relevant migration plan before adding it.
- When replacing an existing Python runtime path, preserve its behavior with
  Rust tests and collected `unittest.TestCase` parity coverage until the
  approved rollback/observation window permits fixture cleanup.
